  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_ae0f42a8af694254b11af0af0c802f68",
      "statement": "The Smart Tutor backend uses a modules-first layout inside one Python package (`smart_tutor`): each feature module contains `domain/`, `application/`, `ports/`, and `adapters/` sub-packages plus a `README.md`. The eleven feature modules are: knowledge, subjects, tutoring, learning, accounts, insights, graph, catalog, quizzes, recommendations, and reports.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L7-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1e5541913040eca686ba1eb9cc187a04a5e087db06cbb7dba6b1d6fc04147d34:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/adr/0001-modular-monolith.md#L12-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5060c0c96da0245cc45baa5f89f3399c99aa49859b0b004b3c2b0c1392706621:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/specs/2026-10-02-project-structure-design.md#L106-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06434f1c795fee4d451e66a349b9a84c227224fb6dc4d69823fab9dd61b739cf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e6c95e6e2c0642f5beac878b0d997701",
      "statement": "Within each module, `domain/` holds entities and business rules with no I/O; `application/` holds one service per use case and acts as the module's public API; `ports/` holds ABCs; and `adapters/` holds vendor SDK implementations and is the only place vendor SDKs may appear.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L24-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7010fc38265afb08c0874a94adec30b48a4feab9ac4f8edd5a05dd52345b521f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/specs/2026-10-02-project-structure-design.md#L106-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06434f1c795fee4d451e66a349b9a84c227224fb6dc4d69823fab9dd61b739cf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c0f8a6f43032438482e6963e8b62b768",
      "statement": "`apps/` contains one composition root per deployable (api, agent, mcp_server, worker, jobs). Entrypoints parse input, call one application service, and format output; no business rules live in `apps/`. Nothing imports `apps/` — it is a leaf.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L21-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6b10f4f020aa4821f56af41b157551ca5371797357860b0ba886918e55078abf:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/pyproject.toml#L351-L368",
