          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4ec162bd0c83fd6d4cbd7b01854489e34148166653cb5d766d92acdf844e40cc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_545fe7ea34204f09a87c7fdbc6edc6e9",
      "statement": "Cross-module flows that go against the acyclic dependency order are orchestrated in `apps/` rather than through a reverse import. The canonical example is 'Discuss this note': `apps/api` reads the note from `learning.application.NoteService` then starts a thread via `tutoring.application.AskService`, keeping neither module importing the other.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L32-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d1cd870559ed3bee2f0ea2f3aaadc52b6a00786399d664e49be89bb24187304:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/adr/0001-modular-monolith.md#L19-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7ac51faa977bcdbe588a9007e42ed7c7f823c708419e2170d1c6f5fdc027948:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/specs/2026-10-02-project-structure-design.md#L133-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7f2e01f8f2f20c0bb6fbb3da9eda4d246adbe208d25685a50942d8099c5686e5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f8f7fcce3ef94a5aa53074a7638845cb",
      "statement": "The acyclic module dependency order (top imports bottom, never the reverse) is: reports → recommendations → quizzes | catalog → learning → tutoring → graph → knowledge → subjects → accounts | insights. `accounts` and `insights` are independent siblings, as are `quizzes` and `catalog`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L43-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45bbe5c5511b9b83510be61b85552e8d57b6bdde4deb09c643215e3e2ddff9bc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/pyproject.toml#L443-L460",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:91be039ffbe41240c7e7232608f3573f3539dafdcb14bf4ba3acd1646592580d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/adr/0004-subjects-module.md#L14-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fe58cdb030bdba566457c64d89b05b7156ed6a7667ebbdfc7d2fd71aa1c1582:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/specs/2026-10-02-project-structure-design.md#L139-L145",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:414ae8e236f30bef24ec14bd604f0e55661d966ba14f175753443f51840c1df3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c75495631464e7388d89cdcd0ca0305",
      "statement": "CI enforces 18 import-linter contracts via `PYTHONUTF8=1 uv run lint-imports`. The contracts fall into five categories: (1) layers inside each module, (2) module privacy — cross-module access only via `application`, (3) apps as leaves, (4) vendor SDK confinement — docling only in `knowledge.adapters`, boto3/langgraph/mcp only in `adapters` or `apps`, (5) the acyclic module dependency graph. A broken contract fails the build.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L37-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45a038c54c85422eeee9250d2927c9cb209821bc64bc4f5c5387087dea85607f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/pyproject.toml#L71-L460",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e391d1e1124f37c175a9bf665b144fffdc008bfda9579ce1b7267483fabf4b9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/adr/0001-modular-monolith.md#L15-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5f6dd3b6067c6ceb3a171e7243d27b61293a5ea3c22cd15f5e6dffc6927a0be:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a62db93fca7749c0b903cd9d4b3788db",
      "statement": "`docling` is forbidden everywhere except `knowledge.adapters` because it pulls in PyTorch and is installed only in the `worker` image via the `[ingest]` optional dependency group. All other modules and `apps` are prohibited from importing it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L42-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20b0e0f0d2353077687629da58b92dbd73cbd8950c1d40de8a1cf6430586af38:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/pyproject.toml#L26-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f16bc6ce9a901b095a1235833f358d57614d75adf94c8c8d92a4d744456ec90c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/pyproject.toml#L424-L441",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e1fb7bc0ced619b8904a1fb2280034edd1037b19c624ddb962287c6d5dc44d92:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_535248db40b046dbb5319ea10be7a079",
      "statement": "The `shared` kernel is open to all modules but imports no feature module and no `apps`. It holds cross-module value objects (UserId, ThreadId, TokenUsage, Citation), model ports (ChatModel, EmbeddingModel, Clock), ModelFactory, authentication, and infrastructure clients.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L11-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ae7c74dc2a521110eddf9c482628bd96aa6c94ffe040bb10f0f8872bf30a83d0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/pyproject.toml#L332-L349",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c8999689bc241d60e6f46b35b06eacd923e3a5567a5051fcb97f1bb8a4865059:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/specs/2026-10-02-project-structure-design.md#L76-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a889fee1d8422d993cbc9675d89e3f2b3f7ecf337118c2d72b1be9ab3eea293e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5c4a83cee56646c590279c8982e873e5",
      "statement": "The agent retrieval path never accesses chunk tables directly: `tutoring`'s `Retriever` port is implemented as an MCP-client adapter calling `apps/mcp_server`, which calls `knowledge.application.SearchService`. This keeps chunk-table access inside `knowledge`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L44-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:40133403c46d570f7a6df8ca3c91f58058a1195fb1d36556bbf7f1d21fb1fad3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/specs/2026-10-02-project-structure-design.md#L133-L133",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d4b2f8166847d6e60dce0fc372e7eec6fc564863ba690b7b0d4cf0aedafc6deb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_91d224ca3cad4ff6aa97f7026746ecda",
      "statement": "A new cross-module dependency that requires changing the module dependency order must be introduced intentionally with a PR explanation; the correct remediation for a broken import-linter contract is always to fix the dependency direction, never to suppress the linter.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L46-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee0ff4e1d86c05d9527dd3f63181d8446b02e817093ecbc61871e676cef8c754:"
        },
        {
