        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4895162b553945cf860d11d44e8b23fe",
      "statement": "Rule 1 is implemented as two separate `layers` contracts: one with `containers` set to all eleven feature modules enforcing `adapters | application → ports → domain`, and one separate contract for `smart_tutor.shared` enforcing `adapters → ports → domain` (shared has no `application` sub-package).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/pyproject.toml#L76-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:833f5bd476a87c23f4878212819b60ecb2c4ca7435bd609ba5e48a45e2556f82:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0a742ab3fb7243a884c5d7a8eb44b5f0",
      "statement": "Rule 2 is implemented as twelve `forbidden` contracts: one for each of the eleven feature modules (knowledge, subjects, tutoring, learning, accounts, insights, catalog, quizzes, recommendations, reports, graph) forbidding external access to their `domain`, `ports`, and `adapters`, plus one contract for `shared` forbidding it from importing any feature module or `apps`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/pyproject.toml#L100-L349",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8e34182e8c4d03a6c9eb58ceb3762d0a7b1ee712abceb5c0699da45a4f0e30d0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_168c49a371e1469ba317137b767cf9d6",
      "statement": "When `lint-imports` detects a violation it prints the contract name and the exact import chain that broke it (e.g., `smart_tutor.learning.application.note_service -> smart_tutor.tutoring.domain.thread`), then reports how many contracts are broken. The correct fix is always to move the offending code (into `adapters/`, through a port, or orchestrate in `apps/`), never to relax the contract.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/AGENTS.md#L37-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f98c15400746c2f1547257ff32817ae41ce5ad974da7159f42fd1e248d0e3f5a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/pyproject.toml#L66-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0d17e50ec5d7a2078966a30deb5cb4c803186267ef6cee841bcbd60d166eb8c:"
        }
      ]
    }
